  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# 3.14.0.4\n\nThe Microsoft.Extensions integration becomes its own package, and `DatadogNet.Maui` gains a\nWindows stub head — which together remove the last pieces of ceremony this set asked of an app.\nThe binding pins are unchanged: DatadogNet.iOS `3.14.0.2` (dd-sdk-ios 3.14.0), DatadogNet.Android\n`3.12.1.2` (dd-sdk-android 3.12.1), DatadogNet.Mac `3.14.0.1`.\n\n## New: `DatadogNet.Extensions.DependencyInjection`\n\nEverything `UseDatadog` wired into the container now lives in a package with no MAUI in it, so a\nplain .NET Android or iOS app, a background service, or a test host gets the same wiring:\n\n```csharp\nbuilder.Services.AddDatadog(new DatadogConfiguration { /* … */ });   // init + registrations\nbuilder.Logging.AddDatadog();                                        // the ILogger provider\nbuilder.Services.AddHttpClient<OrderService>().AddDatadogTracking(); // HttpClient instrumentation\n```\n\n`AddDatadog` registers `IRumMonitor`, `IDatadogLogs`, `IDatadogLogger`, `IDatadogTracer` and\n`ISessionReplay` as singletons with `TryAdd` semantics (a test host's fake wins); an overload\nwithout the configuration registers without initialising, for apps that initialise the SDK even\nearlier. `DatadogNet.Maui` depends on this package and delegates to it — a MAUI app changes\nnothing and gets the same behaviour through `UseDatadog`.\n\n**Moves to be aware of** (source-compatible for a typical app, which already has\n`using DatadogNet;`):\n\n- `AddDatadogTracking` and `DatadogHttpMessageHandlerOptions` moved from the `DatadogNet.Maui`\n  namespace and assembly into `DatadogNet` in the new package.\n- The `ILoggingBuilder.AddDatadog(DatadogMauiOptions?)` overload is replaced by\n  `AddDatadog(LoggerOptions?, LogLevel)` in the new package; `UseDatadog` passes the MAUI\n  options' values through, so only direct callers of the old overload adjust.\n\n## `DatadogNet.Maui` restores on a Windows head\n\nThe package now ships `net8.0/net9.0/net10.0-windows10.0.19041.0` stub heads: `UseDatadog`\ncompiles and runs on a Windows head, and every call lands in the core package's documented no-op\nneutral implementation. The platform-conditional `PackageReference` that earlier releases\nrequired for a windows-headed app is no longer needed — every package in the set is referenced\nunconditionally.\n\n## Unhandled-exception coverage reaches the platform boundaries\n\nBeyond `AppDomain.UnhandledException` and `TaskScheduler.UnobservedTaskException`, the reporter\nnow hooks Android's `UnhandledExceptionRaiser` and Apple's managed-exception marshalling (iOS and\nMac Catalyst) — the boundaries where a failure can end the app without ever reaching the\n`AppDomain` hook. A weak reported-set ensures a failure seen by more than one hook is one RUM\nerror, not two.\n\n## Verified harder\n\n- The device tests now exercise `DatadogNet.WebView` on a **real platform web view** — bridge in,\n  bridge out, plus the argument contract — where previously the package was never executed\n  anywhere.\n- The sample gains the missing demonstrations: a tracked WebView page, a `ConfigureNative`\n  worked example (one platform-only setting per side), a consent cycle, and the consent-gated\n  `StartRecordingImmediately = false` → `StartRecording()` flow.\n- The `DatadogNet.WebView` and `DatadogNet.CrashReporting` packages ship the Android R8\n  keep-rules for their JNI-only entry points under `buildTransitive/` — the binding packages'\n  own rules cannot flow through this set's `exclude=Build` dependencies — asserted by a new\n  package test. Six new unit tests cover the DI package's registrations, `TryAdd` semantics,\n  provider de-duplication and the HttpClient wiring.\n\n## Release pipeline\n\nnuget.org now shows these notes (`docs/release-notes/<version>.md` packs into\n`PackageReleaseNotes`); CI fails when the README's versions drift from `Directory.Build.props` —\nthe install snippets sat at `3.14.0.1` while `3.14.0.3` shipped, and cannot do that again. The\nnet8 sunset is stated policy: dropped in the first release after .NET 8 leaves support on\n**10 November 2026**, in step with the binding repositories.\n\n## Upgrading from 3.14.0.3\n\nFor a MAUI app: nothing to change; optionally delete any windows-head guard around the\n`DatadogNet.Maui` reference. Direct callers of the moved HttpClient/logging extensions: see the\nmoves above.",
